{"content":[{"c":["FORDS OF THE JORDAN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Shallow places where people and animals could wade through the Jordan River. Many OT personalities crossed over the Jordan at its two main fords: these people include Jacob (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.32.10","r":"Gen.32.10","rawR":"Gen.32.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.32.10","value":"Gen.32.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 32:10"},"), Gideon (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.8.4","r":"Judg.8.4","rawR":"Judg.8.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.8.4","value":"Judg.8.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 8:4"},"), David (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.10.17","r":"2Sam.10.17","rawR":"2Sam.10.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.10.17","value":"2Sam.10.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 10:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.17.22","r":"2Sam.17.22","rawR":"2Sam.17.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.17.22","value":"2Sam.17.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"17:22"},"), Absalom (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.17.24","r":"2Sam.17.24","rawR":"2Sam.17.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.17.24","value":"2Sam.17.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"17:24"},"), Abner and his men (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.2.29","r":"2Sam.2.29","rawR":"2Sam.2.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.2.29","value":"2Sam.2.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:29"},"). Joshua led his followers across the Jordan on dry land during a flood, truly a God-given miracle (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.3.15-16","r":"Josh.3.15-16","rawR":"Josh.3.15-16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.3.15-16","value":"Josh.3.15-16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 3:15-16"},"). Jesus crossed the Jordan on several occasions on his trips between Galilee and Jerusalem."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["The two main fords of the Jordan were at Jericho (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.2.7","r":"Josh.2.7","rawR":"Josh.2.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.2.7","value":"Josh.2.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 2:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.3.28","r":"Judg.3.28","rawR":"Judg.3.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.3.28","value":"Judg.3.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 3:28"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.19.15","r":"2Sam.19.15","rawR":"2Sam.19.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.19.15","value":"2Sam.19.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 19:15"},") and at Bethabara, where John baptized (",{"href":"?bref=John.1.28","r":"John.1.28","rawR":"John.1.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.1.28","value":"John.1.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 1:28"},", ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). In certain places and at certain times the Jordan was not fordable: after the melting of the snows in the Lebanon Mountains, and near the Dead Sea, where the Jordan is about 100 feet (30.5 meters) wide and from 5 to 10 feet (1.5 to 3 meters) deep (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.3.15","r":"Josh.3.15","rawR":"Josh.3.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.3.15","value":"Josh.3.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 3:15"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=JordanRiver_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"JordanRiver_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"JordanRiver_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Jordan River"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"FordsoftheJordan","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 32:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.32.10","rawQueryValue":"Gen.32.10","sourceRefExact":"Gen.32.10"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 8:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.8.4","rawQueryValue":"Judg.8.4","sourceRefExact":"Judg.8.4"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 10:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.10.17","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.10.17","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.10.17"},{"anchorText":"17:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.17.22","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.17.22","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.17.22"},{"anchorText":"17:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.17.24","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.17.24","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.17.24"},{"anchorText":"2:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.2.29","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.2.29","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.2.29"},{"anchorText":"Jos 3:15-16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.3.15-16","rawQueryValue":"Josh.3.15-16","sourceRefExact":"Josh.3.15-16"},{"anchorText":"Jos 2:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.2.7","rawQueryValue":"Josh.2.7","sourceRefExact":"Josh.2.7"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 3:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.3.28","rawQueryValue":"Judg.3.28","sourceRefExact":"Judg.3.28"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 19:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.19.15","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.19.15","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.19.15"},{"anchorText":"Jn 1:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=John.1.28","rawQueryValue":"John.1.28","sourceRefExact":"John.1.28"},{"anchorText":"Jos 3:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.3.15","rawQueryValue":"Josh.3.15","sourceRefExact":"Josh.3.15"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"6e247c37b2c6e186c2ecd6145b7ef4786ac35747563c4751e8ca833f294f2d7c","sourceItemName":"FordsoftheJordan","sourceItemOrder":62,"sourceMember":"Articles/F.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"FordsoftheJordan","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Fords of the Jordan","title":"Fords of the Jordan","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}